{"name":"Willow Grove","hex":"#69755c","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Willow Grove","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A town in the Shire of Baw Baw, south eastern Victoria, Australia.","A settlement in Simonds parish, Saint John County, New Brunswick, Canada."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Willow_Grove"}],"entries":[{"title":"Willow Grove (Greensboro, Maryland)","blocks":[{"text":"Willow Grove is a historic home located at Greensboro, Caroline County, Maryland, United States. It is one of the few Georgian-style houses in Caroline County that were constructed between 1780 and 1790. It is a two-story brick house covered with a thin coat of stucco, measuring 37 feet long and 34 feet deep. It was built by Matthew Driver, Jr., who with three other members from Caroline County ratified the United States Constitution at the State Convention in 1788."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Willow_Grove_(Greensboro%2C_Maryland)"},{"title":"Willow Grove, Delaware","blocks":[{"text":"Willow Grove is an unincorporated community in Kent County, Delaware, United States. Willow Grove is located on Delaware Route 10, southwest of Camden."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Willow_Grove%2C_Delaware"},{"title":"Willow","blocks":[{"text":"Willows, also called sallows and osiers, of the genus Salix, comprise around 350 species of typically deciduous trees and shrubs. They are primarily found on moist soils in cold and temperate regions."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/00/Salix_alba_Morton.jpg/330px-Salix_alba_Morton.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Willow"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1d/Salix_silesiaca_a5.jpg/500px-Salix_silesiaca_a5.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/comm